ls only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Maryland remains one of the most Democratic-leaning states in presidential politics, and the fundamentals point to a double-digit Democratic margin. No incumbent is on the ballot once the term-limited Republican president leaves office, so neither side carries an incumbency edge. No public polls of Maryland, expert ratings, or market prices are available for this race, so the forecast rests on the state's underlying partisan lean.\n\nRecent headlines from the state focus on congressional primaries, the race to succeed Steny Hoyer, Governor Wes Moore's re-election, and Democratic redistricting efforts, none of which suggests the presidential contest is in doubt. Maryland's Democratic margins in recent presidential cycles have run well ahead of its partisan lean, and a popular Democratic governor heads the state ticket. The Democrat is a heavy favorite, though the absence of polling keeps uncertainty wider than in well-surveyed states.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9506, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9102, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9258, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9194, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9194, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9136, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9144, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9103, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9184, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9155, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9262, "margin": 16.0}]}